# Pinned OpenSSL engine (ADR-001). Sourced by scripts/build-openssl.sh, the
# release workflow, and asserted by tests/engine.
#
# Update policy (ADR-007): check
# https://openssl-library.org/news/vulnerabilities/ regularly and before each
# release. If the pinned version is affected, bumping it here is top priority.
#
# 3.5.x is the LTS branch (EOL 2030-04-08) and is the first release with native
# ML-KEM / ML-DSA / SLH-DSA in the default provider.
#
# 3.5.8 (2026-08-25) is the latest released 3.5.x patch and has no known
# unpatched vulnerability. It is a security release: it closes CVE-2026-63072
# (heap buffer overflow in CMS key unwrapping), CVE-2026-75803 (AEAD forgeries
# with empty ciphertext via EVP_Cipher), CVE-2026-63073/63074/63076 (CMP),
# CVE-2026-54874 (DTLS), CVE-2026-14457 (RPK), and the QUIC-server issues
# CVE-2026-18798 / 14456 / 63075. Most severe is Moderate.
#
# Bumped from 3.5.7 on 2026-08-25, the day 3.5.8 was released. 3.5.7 was
# affected by all of the above; only the QUIC ones were unreachable from this
# project's subprocess usage, so the CMS and AEAD fixes are the reason this is
# not a cosmetic bump.
OPENSSL_VERSION=3.5.8
OPENSSL_SHA256=a8f84a39918ec6415ce765d9b429d313ba97b8143169c172e734b9514464f5b2
